[Applause]  come on  thank you in what's being called heroics  of New York's finest body camera video  shows NYPD officers rescue a man who  fell on a Manhattan train track just  seconds before the train arrived  thank you  it happened on November 24th at the East  116th and Lexington Avenue Station at  the time NYPD officers Brunel Victor and  to puke booze were conducting a Transit  sweep when they were told a man fell  onto the tracks body camera video shows  officers rushing for the tracks where  the man had fallen they arrived to find  another person had already jumped onto  the tracks in an effort to help the man  back onto the platform with the help of  that Good Samaritan officers lit the man  off the tracks  body camera video then shows one of the  officers attempt to hoist himself up  onto the platform but fall back that's  when the Good Samaritan grabs his hand  seconds after everyone was removed from  the tracks the train arrives at the  station  officials say the man who fell in the  tracks may have had a medical issue  after he was rescued another responding  officer provided Medical Aid until  additional First Responders arrived the  man was then taken to the hospital with  minor injuries  the police commissioner kishan Sewell  tweeted a video of the rescue saying the  officers courage is quote second nature  for the latest developments in this  story and all things True Crime stay  with long crime Network I'm Sierra  Gillespie

